=== README.md ===
# Infrastructure

This repository describes the Cloudflare setup of the site or sites it was made for, as code.

## What is here

- `imports.tf` and the `modules/` folders describe what already exists on Cloudflare. Nothing here creates it again.
- `backend.tf` keeps the record of what Terraform manages in Cloudflare R2, encrypted.
- `IMPORT-REPORT.md` lists what was brought in and what was left alone.
- `.github/workflows/infra.yml` plans each pull request and applies a change only after it is approved.

## Secrets

Set these in the repository's settings. Their values are never written to a file.

- `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`: the Cloudflare token the workflow uses.
- `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` and `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`: the R2 keys for the record of changes.
- `STATE_ENCRYPTION_PASSPHRASE`: encrypts that record.
- `EDITS_RUNNER_TOKEN`: lets the workflow report each plan back to Keep Shipping.
- `EMAIL_ROUTING_DESTINATIONS`: the email forwarding addresses, as one JSON object keyed by rule.

The Cloudflare account id and the console's address are not secrets: the workflow file carries them.

## Test environment

The test environment has its own folder, `modules/test-env/`. If it uses a database, its address, port, name, user and password are secrets named `TEST_DB_HOST`, `TEST_DB_PORT`, `TEST_DB_DATABASE`, `TEST_DB_USER` and `TEST_DB_PASSWORD`.
=== backend.tf ===
terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    key = "acct123/kaje/terraform.tfstate"
    region = "auto"
    endpoints = {
      s3 = "https://acct123.r2.cloudflarestorage.com"
    }
    use_lockfile = true
    skip_credentials_validation = true
    skip_region_validation = true
    skip_requesting_account_id = true
    skip_metadata_api_check = true
    skip_s3_checksum = true
    use_path_style = true
  }
  encryption {
    key_provider "pbkdf2" "state" {
      passphrase = var.state_encryption_passphrase
    }
    method "aes_gcm" "state" {
      keys = key_provider.pbkdf2.state
    }
    state {
      method = method.aes_gcm.state
      enforced = true
    }
    plan {
      method = method.aes_gcm.state
      enforced = true
    }
  }
}

variable "state_encryption_passphrase" {
  description = "Passphrase for the OpenTofu state encryption, supplied through the Secrets port as TF_VAR_state_encryption_passphrase."
  type        = string
  sensitive   = true
}
